            "review_title": "Review at Furyu Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Nikki Nguyen\n10 contributions\n0\nBest bang for the buck Japanese place in Hanoi\nAug 2017 • Family\nI was a regular at this place called Furyu Ramen shop for years, their main audience were the Japanese expats so you really don't see many Vietnamese customers there, ever customer was a regular and the service was family-oriented. Then one day they expanded and opened up a bigger joint and their menu now has expanded to sashimi and sushi. Having known the Chef for a long time (since the Ramen days), I know for a fact that their fish are 'legals', imported, with all the quality certificates and everything, they also only consume the fish in the day (without serving it on the next day) so the sashimi is superbly fresh. This is one of my concerns regarding Japanese food in hanoi as I've heard many concerns about hygiene and safety. \n\nApart from the food, which is always wonderful the most incredible thing is probably the price - it's one of the least expensive Japanese places I've been to and makes a great place for family dining. However, don't expect to get the fine dining service, as I said, this is a family run business and the servers are nice, respectful, welcoming but definitely not the typical servers you see in fancy places. \n\nHappy eating!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 7, 2017",
